{
  "description": "#5395 — a journal day is born with the space's journal template, whoever creates it. The frontend used to copy the template itself, and only when the journal view created the day; a day Quick Capture or the MCP `journal_for_date` tool created first stayed empty, and opening it later added nothing because the page already existed. The copy now lives in the backend: `create_page_in_space` on a date title (the journal view's and the date picker's creator) and `resolve_or_create_journal_page` (Quick Capture, `journal_for_date`) both call `apply_journal_template_in_tx` inside the page's own transaction, so one undo reverts the day and its template together.\n\nThe template is the live page flagged `journal-template = true` with the smallest id, copied as Duplicate copies a subtree: content with nesting, the block's own ops in order (`create_block` per block, properties after it). The variables expand against the DAY being created, not the clock: `<% today %>`, `<% page title %>`, `{{date}}` and `{{title}}` are the day, `{{cursor}}` goes. `<% time %>` is the clock and so cannot be pinned here; `quick_capture_block` stays waived for the same reason (the local date names the page).\n\nThe title gate is pinned by the last op: a page named `Project` in the same space is born empty. What the mock approximates: it copies content and nesting only, where the backend carries properties and task stamps too; the template here has none.",
